<!-- wp:mbn-theme/location-detailed-page {"whyChooseIntro":"Hastings and Hastings is a Phoenix and Mesa personal injury law firm with the experience and knowledge to effectively advocate for you and your family. We've been serving Arizona accident victims and their families for more than 40 years, and our Mesa injury lawyers have almost 100 years of combined experience handling personal injury lawsuits, <a href="/mesa-truck-accident-lawyer/" data-type="link" data-id="/mesa-truck-accident-lawyer/">including truck accident cases</a>.","whyChooseItems":[{"heading":"Proven Track Record from Real Clients","paragraph":"Our track record is evident not only through the cases that we’ve won but in the reviews and referrals that we receive from our clients. We have more than 600 real, handwritten reviews and more than 500 five-star Google reviews from verified, actual past clients. In this business, we hope that we don’t see our clients more than once – as accidents are an unwelcome occurrence to anyone – but most of our business comes from word of mouth, through referrals from past clients who have been satisfied with our team’s work and our representation.","imageId":0,"imageUrl":"","imageFallback":"","imageAlt":""},{"heading":"Innovative Discount Fee Structure","paragraph":"Otherwise, our fee structure sets Hastings and Hastings apart from other personal injury law firms. Usually, a personal injury lawyer charges clients a flat percentage rate of one-third, regardless of the amount of compensation their clients receive. At Hastings and Hastings, we realized that this traditional arrangement benefits lawyers more than it benefits clients, and so we pioneered Discount Fees for our clients. Under our <a href="/discount/">Discount Fee arrangement</a>, we prioritize putting the most amount of money possible back into our clients’ pockets – not our own.","imageId":0,"imageUrl":"","imageFallback":"badge-no-fee.svg","imageAlt":"No Fee Until We Win badge"},{"heading":"Licensed Arizona Personal Injury Attorneys Handling Your Case","paragraph":"Hastings and Hastings also prioritizes getting our clients face-to-face with an actual, licensed Arizona attorney from the very start of our representation. At some personal injury law firms, prospective clients may not speak to a licensed attorney until after their representation has begun. But at Hastings and Hastings, we guarantee that you will speak to a licensed attorney at your free initial consultation – at the very first contact you have with our law firm. These initial consultations with our attorneys are always offered at no cost and with absolutely no risk to our prospective clients. ","imageId":0,"imageUrl":"","imageFallback":"img-team.png","imageAlt":"Hastings and Hastings legal team"}],"howWeHelpIntro":"In the moments immediately following an accident, your legal options likely aren't the first thing on your mind, and for obvious reasons. Instead, you're likely thinking of the most important things – the safety and well-being of yourself and your loved ones. But in the days, months, and weeks following an accident, you will likely quickly realize that the accident's aftereffects are much larger than you might have planned for.","howWeHelpItems":[{"text":"Accidents are expensive. In obtaining medical treatment, victims rack up significant expenses in hospital bills, insurance copays, medication, transportation, and doctor office visits. Additionally, many victims are unable to work, leading to lost wages and in some cases, loss of employment entirely. Victims may have suffered property damage, even damage and injury from riding a bicycle as well as in the form of a totaled car, damage to their home, or loss of belongings. Some medical emergency may include loss of limbs, which is where the best Mesa amputation injury lawyer will be the main point of contact.","imageId":0,"imageUrl":"","imageFallback":"accident-ambulance.jpg","imageAlt":"Multi-vehicle accident scene with ambulance at night","imagePosition":"left"},{"text":"Long story short, accidents are incredibly expensive for victims. Lawsuits allow victims to recover the money they've lost due to the negligence or carelessness of another person or company. A personal injury lawyer's entire purpose is assisting victims in accessing the funds to which they are legally entitled, so a victim is fully and fairly compensated for the injuries they have suffered.","imageId":0,"imageUrl":"","imageFallback":"billing-statement.jpg","imageAlt":"Medical billing statement with stethoscope","imagePosition":"right"}],"caseCategoriesSubtitle":"Our team at Hastings and Hastings has extensive experience handling personal injury lawsuits of every type and scope. While each Mesa injury case is different and presents its own set of facts, Arizona law underpinning personal injury cases is often the same across each case. Over the course of the last 40 years, our <a href="/mesa-car-accident-attorney/">Mesa car accident attorneys</a> have built a proven track record of success in representing Arizona personal injury victims, including <a href="/mesa-brain-injury-lawyer/">our specialized Mesa brain injury lawyer,</a> and our familiarity with the law of personal injuries speaks for itself. We also have the <a href="/chandler-car-accident-attorney/">best representation at our Chandler car accident attorney office</a>.","caseCategoriesClosing":"In addition to these types of cases, our team is willing to consider any type of personal injury lawsuit. Since we have some of the best weather and beautiful lakes, we also offer the <a href="/mesa-boat-accident-attorney/">best Mesa Boat accident attorney in the area</a>. In other words, if you have found yourself injured due to the wrongful acts or omissions of another person, company, or group of people, we want to hear from you. Our free consultations are offered at no cost and no risk to prospective clients, and our team is ready to listen to your story.","testimonials":[{"quote":"Hastings and Hastings handled my claim after I had tried to deal with insurance company myself.","authorName":"Verified Client","authorRole":"Car Accident Victim","rating":5},{"quote":"I was in a car accident a few months ago and could not be happier with the outcome. Sean Hennick, my attorney, along with all the other staff at Hastings and Hastings, were extremely professional and helpful. Having Hastings and Hastings by my side made this process seem easy. I would highly recommend Hastings and Hastings to anyone I know.","authorName":"Verified Client","authorRole":"Car Accident Victim","rating":5},{"quote":"They are great! They do preliminary questions to make sure that you aren't wasting your time (or theirs). They stand up for you and do what is right for you. Can't say enough positive comments on how they handled my case. They are responsive to emails and follow up. They only take legitimate cases and don't subscribe to "frivolous" lawsuits.","authorName":"Verified Client","authorRole":"Injury Victim","rating":4},{"quote":"I can't say how happy I am with Hastings & Hastings right now. I came to them about 9 months ago after my accident and today I received my settlement. Everyone there was very nice and helpful. My attorney's paralegal always responded to my emails quickly which really impressed me. I'm so pleased with my experience with them that I had to write a review!","authorName":"Verified Client","authorRole":"Accident Victim","rating":5}],"faqItems":[{"question":"Q. How Do I Know If I Have a Personal Injury Case?","answer":"<p>To determine if you have a personal injury case, consider the following factors:</p><p><strong>Injury or Harm:</strong> You must have suffered physical, emotional, or financial harm due to the actions or negligence of another party. This harm could result from accidents, intentional acts, or even defective products.<br><strong>Fault or Negligence:</strong> You need to establish that someone else's actions or negligence caused or contributed to your injury. Negligence refers to a failure to exercise reasonable care, leading to harm to others.<br><strong>Duty of Care:</strong> The at-fault party must have owed you a duty of care. For example, in a car accident, drivers have a duty to follow traffic rules and drive safely.<br><strong>Breach of Duty:</strong> You must show that the at-fault party breached their duty of care. In other words, they failed to act in a manner expected under the circumstances.<br><strong>Causation:</strong> You need to demonstrate a direct link between the at-fault party's breach of duty and your injury. The breach must be the cause of your harm.<br><strong>Damages:</strong> You must have suffered quantifiable damages due to the injury, such as medical expenses, lost wages, pain and suffering, or property damage.<br><strong>Time Limit:</strong> Personal injury cases have a statute of limitations, which is the time frame within which you must file your claim. In Arizona, this time limit can vary depending on the type of case.</p><p>If you believe that the above criteria apply to your situation, it's essential to consult with a qualified personal injury attorney. They can evaluate the details of your case, assess its strengths and weaknesses, and advise you on the best course of action. Personal injury attorneys are experienced in handling such cases and can guide you through the legal process to pursue the compensation you may be entitled to for your injuries and losses. Keep in mind that each case is unique, so seeking professional legal advice is crucial to understanding your specific circumstances.</p>","isOpen":false,"bullets":"<li></li>"},{"question":"Q. Will My Personal Injury Case Be Settled Out of Court?","answer":"<p>Most personal injury cases in Arizona are settled out of court. However, the specific outcome depends on the facts and circumstances of each case. Our attorneys are prepared to take your case to trial if a fair settlement cannot be reached.</p>","isOpen":false},{"question":"Q. What Evidence Will I Need For My Mesa Personal Injury Lawyer?","answer":"<p>Important evidence includes medical records, photographs of the accident scene and injuries, witness statements, police reports, and documentation of lost wages and expenses. Your attorney will help gather and preserve evidence on your behalf.</p>","isOpen":false}],"badgesItems":[{"imageId":10028,"imageUrl":"http://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/badge-90-plus-combined-legal-experience-blck.svg","imageFallback":"badge-90-plus-combined-legal-experience-blck.svg","imageAlt":"90+ Years Combined Legal Experience badge","imageWidth":303,"imageHeight":303},{"imageId":9916,"imageUrl":"http://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/badge-29-percent-diiscount.svg","imageFallback":"badge-29-percent-discount.svg","imageAlt":"29% Fee — Discount Accident Lawyers badge","imageWidth":303,"imageHeight":303}],"servingColumns":[{"title":"Central & Historic Mesa","links":[{"label":"Historic District","url":"#"},{"label":"Fraser Fields","url":"#"},{"label":"Reed Park","url":"#"},{"label":"Kleinman Park","url":"#"}]},{"title":"East Mesa","links":[{"label":"Apache Wells","url":"#"},{"label":"Eastmark","url":"#"},{"label":"Mulberry","url":"#"},{"label":"Superstition Springs","url":"#"}]},{"title":"South & West Mesa","links":[{"label":"Dobson Ranch","url":"#"},{"label":"Fiesta Park Village","url":"#"},{"label":"Carriage Manor","url":"#"},{"label":"Sherwood Manor","url":"#"}]},{"title":"Surrounding Mesa Communities","links":[{"label":"Community Fiesta","url":"#"},{"label":"Fountain of the Sun","url":"#"},{"label":"Holden Rock","url":"#"},{"label":"Northgrove","url":"#"},{"label":"Nuestro","url":"#"},{"label":"Santa Rita Ranch","url":"#"},{"label":"Water Improvement","url":"#"},{"label":"C.A.N.D.O.","url":"#"}]}],"faultIntroText":"Oftentimes, accidents are not simple matters. Things can quickly become complicated when the question arises of who is truly responsible for an accident that occurred. Making matters worse, a significant amount of misinformation exists about how the specific circumstances of an accident may affect liability. No matter what you may have heard, speaking to a licensed Arizona attorney is the only way to know for sure if you may be entitled to compensation, and if so, in what amount.","faultIntroImageId":10000,"faultIntroImageUrl":"http://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/img-determining-fault-accident-scene.jpg","faultComparativeColumn1":"Arizona is a "comparative negligence" state, which means that even plaintiffs who were slightly negligent themselves may be able to recover compensation for injuries they suffered in an accident. <a href="https://www.azleg.gov/ars/12/02505.htm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Comparative negligence</a> is a complicated legal doctrine, and speaking to an experienced Mesa personal injury attorney is the best way to ensure that the law is most effectively being applied to your injury case. But the following example provides a basic hypothetical to illustrate how competitive negligence works:<br><br>Imagine that you are driving on the highway in Mesa, and the speed limit is 75 miles per hour. You are in the left lane with your cruise control set to 80 miles per hour, or five miles per hour over the speed limit. You are passing a car in the middle lane, when at once, the car veers into the left lane, striking your car.<br><br>The driver of the other vehicle was using FaceTime while driving, listening to the radio at high volume, eating a burger, and their side mirror was broken, hanging off the side of their car with no possible use. The other driver, obviously driving distracted, came into your lane without checking to see whether it was clear.<br><br>After filing a lawsuit, the other driver claims that you caused the accident by speeding. What happens next?<br><br>Your car was totaled in the accident, and you suffered significant injuries.","faultComparativeColumn2":"After filing a lawsuit, the other driver claims that you caused the accident by speeding. What happens next?<br><br>In this hypothetical injury case, while the other driver may be partially correct in noting that you were speeding, it is clear that the other driver was significantly more negligent in their own actions, driving while extremely distracted, and without a working side mirror.<br><br>Comparative negligence allows a jury to determine exactly what percentage of fault can be apportioned to each party involved in a lawsuit and determine how to award damages accordingly. In this case, a jury might say that the plaintiff's speeding contributed to 10 percent of the accident's occurrence. Thus, if the same jury awarded the plaintiff damages, those damages would be reduced by 10 percent – allowing them to still recover, but in an amount reduced by their own contributions to the accident.<br><br>What does this mean for Mesa accident victims? It means that even if you believe you may have contributed to an accident occurring, you should still consult a Mesa injury attorney. Arizona's comparative negligence law may still allow you to recover for your injuries, and our team at Hastings and Hastings has extensive experience in handling these complicated matters. ","faultCompensationSubtitle":"The types of damages that are available to Mesa accident victims depend on the specific facts of each individual case. But in general, under Arizona law, accident victims are able to recover damages that are both economic and non-economic in nature.","faultStepsSubtitle":"Being involved in an accident often leaves victims unsure about how to move forward. In the unfortunate event that you find yourself or a loved one injured due to another person's negligence, you should think about these steps:","faultTimeLimitParagraph1":"One of the biggest reasons that it is imperative you speak to a lawyer as soon as possible after an accident occurs is because of the statute of limitations.","faultTimeLimitParagraph2":"The statute of limitations is a law that places a deadline on the amount of time for filing a lawsuit after an incident occurs. In personal injury cases, Arizona's statute of limitations is two years from the date of an accident.","faultTimeLimitImageId":10001,"faultTimeLimitImageUrl":"http://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/img-determining-fault-file-a-claim-1.jpg","faultStatuteImageId":10002,"faultStatuteImageUrl":"http://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/img-determining-fault-file-a-claim-2.jpg","faultStatuteText":"While two years sounds like plenty of time, it's important to note that the deadline applies to the actual filing of a lawsuit in court. Background work, investigation, and preliminary negotiations must occur before a lawsuit is filed, and in some cases, these processes can take months to begin and end. For that reason, it is essential that you consult with an attorney as soon as possible after an accident occurs – the clock is ticking."} /-->

